 "text": "Last year, I finally started learning the piano. I had wanted to play since I was a boy. At first, my fingers felt stiff and slow. Even a simple tune took me a whole week. My teacher gave me one piece of advice that changed everything. Practise for fifteen minutes every day, rather than for two hours once a week. Short, regular practice helps the hands and the mind remember. I now play a little every evening after dinner. I am still a beginner, but I can play several short pieces. Learning an instrument as an adult takes patience, but every small step forward feels like a real reward."
